   "relationship": "Historians of science answer the charge that their field is hostile to or ignorant of science (1996–99)",
   "map_label": "Historians of science reply, 1996–99",
   "evidence_note": "In-period replies by historians of science, read. Steven Shapin, \"Rarely Pure and Never Simple\" (Configurations 7, 1999), writing as \"a historian and a sociologist of science\": methodological relativism \"implies nothing at all about epistemological evaluations or ontological judgments\" (pp. 3–4); the charge of hostility to science or ignorance of it, \"when directed to the work of many distinguished historians and sociologists of science—now deserves to be called by its proper name: it is malevolently misinformed\" (p. 11). He names no protagonist; his target is identified by its arguments, such as Sokal's challenge to jump from a window. John Krige (Physics World, December 1998): Intellectual Impostures \"is essentially a political tract\" and \"lamentably indifferent to the history and philosophy of science\". Mara Beller (Physics Today 51:9, 1998): \"The philosophical pronouncements of Bohr, Born, Heisenberg and Pauli deserve some of the blame for the excesses of the postmodernist critique of science.\" M. Norton Wise reviewed Higher Superstition in Isis (1996; unread); Edge reports his charge of \"a willful strategy of distortion and demonization\" (p. 323). Jardine and Frasca-Spada (SHPS 1997) criticised both sides and are not counted as one-way critics. Not every historian of science sided against the warriors: Margaret Jacob wrote against Latour in A House Built on Sand (1998; see the truthdebate → latour edge). Physicists also criticised historians' method (Weinberg 1996 on Whig history; Sokal and Bricmont 1998, p. 69 n. 88); that thinner charge is not drawn as a sciencewars → science edge.",
   "source_ids": [
    "ss136_shapin_1999",
    "ss136_krige_1998",
    "ss136_beller_1998",
    "ss136_wise_isis_1996",
    "ss136_edge_1997",
    "ss136_jfs_1997"
   ],
   "classification_basis": "editorial_review",
   "review_status": "needs_review",
   "target_strand": "sciencewars/historians_answer",
   "target_strand_note": "historians_answer holds Wise, Jardine, Frasca-Spada, Schweber, Krige, Beller and Shapin.",
   "roster_row": null,
   "include": true
