    "evidence_note": "Comparison only. The disputes overlap in time and in people but neither is a critique of the other. Margaret Jacob took part in both: Telling the Truth about History (1994) already criticised the strong programme and Latour from the historians' side, and she wrote for A House Built on Sand (1998; abstract only). Richard Evans, a truthdebate historian, cited Sokal approvingly in 1999 as having done \"far more effectively and knowledgeably\" what he had only touched on in criticising Derrida and Lyotard. The historians' book predates the Science Wars, and Evans endorses Sokal rather than criticising him, so no critique edge is drawn in either direction. The Science Wars concerned the natural sciences and their students; the truth debate concerned historical writing.",
