    {
      "id": "consumer_chronologies",
      "title": "Competing chronologies and questions",
      "focus": "Compare McKendrick’s eighteenth-century acceleration, Weatherill’s earlier middling ownership and de Vries’s household labor argument. Vickery questions universal motives. Different evidence and outcomes do not yield one automatic date for a consumer society.",
