MEMORY.md:1410:**New user constraint:** User reports Astra and Fable 5.1 top-fifty historians lists contained seven and six women. Treat this as a warning about selection/training bias, not a verified demographic benchmark or proof about training-corpus composition. `REPRESENTATION-REVIEW.md` requires source-grounded audits of discovery, selection and substantive connections across every field, including full nodes versus roster mentions. Women must not be confined to gender history. Model recall, Wikipedia visibility, citation/catalogue counts and degree cannot establish importance. Do not infer gender from names. Every new dossier has a specific representation question; `representation-audit.json` remains pending and blocks production readiness. The 37 harvested author/editor credits are unresolved observations, not distinct people or demographic counts. Digital bibliography recovery lead: Sharon Leon’s chapter on the Great Man narrative; read it before deriving claims.
MEMORY.md:1426:`schema-crosswalk.json` audits all 19 works, 19 consulted witnesses and 20 claims/citation joins from the two unchanged older packets. **Not a completed conversion:** consulted HTML/PDF witnesses need separation from issued publications; contract 0.1 lacks exact critique/revision/contribution/qualification/programme predicates. Preserve these claims and compound strand addresses rather than coercing them into research_connection. Scott's explicit Taylor disagreement and Foucault/Asad method references provide further predicate-design cases, not accepted edges.
MEMORY.md:1498:Most concerns hold with corrections: Thompson’s Moral Economy already has a shared source ID across four rosters, but no normalized work/edition identity. Wehler’s critique already exists as `edge_705` (`bielefeld → micro`); the structural problem is substituting broad endpoints for named actors/strands, not absence of that critique. There are 89 critic selections without `edge_id`, not necessarily 89 missing claims. Source verification is explicitly scoped in prose but not attached to source–claim joins. Local strand IDs can support compound addresses without replacement. Node date fields are synchronized with `date_span`, but title events are not reconciled; three accepted successor titles render “Publication dates unverified.” Historical changes have snapshots/manifests, although no uniform claim lifecycle. Candidate state is mixed into `publication_role`, not `entry_kind`.
